        "description": "A coast-to-coast truck trip, about 2,794 mi, with the default 500-mile tank. It needs several fuel stops.\n\nThe tests walk the trip from start to finish. At each stop they check that the fuel on arrival matches the miles driven since the last one, that gallons = miles of fuel added / mpg and cost = gallons x price, and that the tank is never overfilled. They also check that the last stop buys just enough to reach the finish and that the totals add up.\n\nThe Console prints the walk-through, one line per stop, and the response's **Visualize** tab shows the stops as a table."
      },
